[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_dlg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_dlg")
source = "# Vesper in the Null Zone (Act IV): she goes ahead of you and waits at each zone's entrance.
# She changes as you go deeper: in The Fray she translates; in The Weaver's Loom she finishes the
# Null's sentences before it does; at The Core's Gate she asks you not to kill the Gatekeeper.
# Her lines also follow DECODE THE NULL (the fragments) and the Null Laws (NullLaws).
~ start
@ here:act_4_the_fray -> fray
@ here:act_4_weavers_loom -> loom
@ here:act_4_core_gate -> gate
@ here:act_4_expedition_end -> expedition
@ here:act_4_echo_wells -> wells
-> idle

~ fray
@ quest_done:null_fragments -> fray_fluent
@ recovered:null_fragment_c -> fray_halfway
Vesper: Look at the floor. Those marks aren't damage. They're words.
Vesper: Out here the Null rewrites one of AXIOM's rules at a time. When it does, I'll tell you what I hear.
Vesper: Keep a script set for each rule it breaks. You'll want to swap fast.
* WHAT IS IT SAYING? -> fray_saying
* LET'S GO -> end

~ fray_saying
Vesper: Mostly? Ownership. Every rule it rewrites, it's signing.
-> end

~ fray_halfway
Vesper: You're carrying three of the fragments. Can you feel them? They hum when it speaks.
Vesper: Two more. Then I'll be able to read whole sentences, not just words.
-> end

~ fray_fluent
Vesper: I can read all of it now. I wish I couldn't.
Vesper: It isn't attacking AXIOM. It's correcting it. Every law it rewrites is one we got wrong.
-> end

~ loom
@ quest_done:q07_null_weaver_prime -> loom_after
Vesper: The Weaver speaks the grammar. It'll say a rule: two conditions, joined.
Vesper: Answer in the same rule and it has to let you in. Anything else is just noise to it.
Vesper: And watch the floor. It weaves before it speaks. There's always a gap.
Vesper: ...when they're close, and you're bleeding. Sorry. I keep hearing it before it says it.
* YOU'RE FINISHING ITS SENTENCES -> loom_sentences
* LET'S GO -> end

~ loom_sentences
Vesper: I know. I don't think it minds.
-> end

~ loom_after
Vesper: It's quiet in here now. Quiet in a way that sounds like waiting.
-> end

~ gate
@ quest_done:q08_null_gatekeeper -> gate_after
Vesper: Executor. Before you go in.
Vesper: The Gatekeeper isn't guarding the Core from us. It's guarding the Null from us. From what we'd do to it.
Vesper: I'm asking you not to kill it. I know you will anyway. I just needed to have asked.
* I HAVE TO -> gate_have_to
* I'M SORRY -> gate_sorry

~ gate_have_to
Vesper: I know. Strike it while it's fast. Don't stand in front of it when it's heavy.
-> end

~ gate_sorry
Vesper: Don't be sorry. Be quick. It changes form every few seconds: fast is your window.
-> end

~ gate_after
Vesper: The way is open. It didn't fight to win, at the end. It fought to be heard.
-> end

~ expedition
@ quest_done:guild_expedition -> expedition_after
Vesper: The Guild came this far. Look: their tents are still pitched. They meant to come back.
Vesper: Their examiner is still out there, grading. She won't take sloppy work. Not even from the Null.
Vesper: Lean scripts, Executor. Lean or elegant, or she won't feel a thing.
-> end

~ expedition_after
Vesper: They didn't die here. They stopped. There's a difference, out here.
-> end

~ wells
@ quest_done:static_from_home -> wells_after
Vesper: Listen. Everything that ever fell in here is still talking.
Vesper: There. That's your convoy's call sign. And that's Brack's voice, saying something in a language he doesn't speak.
-> end

~ wells_after
Vesper: It's quieter without your packets in it. The Null kept the echo, though. It keeps everything.
-> end

~ idle
Vesper: Listen. The silence has structure."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dd85gxidfhqxl"
